<title>ARGENTINA: Argentina automaker may set new output stoppages.</title>
<headline>Argentina automaker may set new output stoppages.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine automaker CIADEA SA said Thursday a partial interruption of output for several days this month was due to difficulties its French licensor, Renault, had selling cars in Brazil.</p>
<p>CIADEA added that it could be forced to make more output stoppages in April.</p>
<p>CIADEA's President Manuel Antelo confirmed the reason for the output stoppages was &quot;the revamping of our export program, specifically shipments to Brazil, because of Renault's difficulties in commercial distribution in that country.</p>
</text>
